From 4c691daf50c9e873fec84af0899152cfd587839b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:57:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] CFD turbulence wall details: VRANS wall cells, open
 boundaries, T44 height, wall value, T31, D20 warning

- wallf: VRANS wall-law cells are wall cells (the wall law replaced nothing, the
  bulk production and dissipation were added on top); wave generation, outflow
  and beach boundaries (bc 6/7/8) are no longer wall cells (they lost the bulk
  terms without getting a wall function)
- wall law for k with sediment: the log law is evaluated at the T 44 sampling
  height of the velocity (it used the cell distance); production uses the cell
  velocity
- eps/omega wall value with y >= ks/30, as the k wall law
- k-omega at active wave generation/absorption: limiter T 31 instead of 0.212
- warning for D 20 0 with a turbulence model

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016p5iGZDZyVZVboEfXXfxfV
